   308	def _cleanup_one(iss, rid, doc, now=None):
   309	    """-> True when the obligation is discharged. Content, work files and frames go when the request has ended;
   310	    the receipt goes 30 days after the end (or at once if the request did not complete). Deletion is keyed to the
   311	    persisted end, never to an object's age; objects are tagged cleanup-due just before they are deleted (5.3.1).
   312	
   313	    CF-02: a writer that read the request while it was ACCEPTED (an upload retry, a response consumer, a stale
   314	    poller) may still store an object after the end. Each such writer runs inside one Lambda invocation, so it is
   315	    gone WRITE_LEASE_S after the end was first seen here. Until then the obligation is kept and every poll deletes
   316	    again; only a listing taken after the lease discharges it."""
