   381	    ILC-I6 (owner decision: OLDEST FIRST). Each round receives batches from the slots (each receive a guarded
   382	    request; see below for when it stops), then handles the received messages across slots in order of their sent
   383	    time (SQS SentTimestamp), oldest first. A message left unhandled becomes visible again and grows older. Handling is
   384	    within the drain share (ILC-I2-04): a cooperative allocation checked between messages, never before a round's
   385	    oldest message. Starvation-free with probability 1 only under the capacity condition stated below.
   386	
   387	    Receiving goes on to the next slot only while that receive PLUS one message's complete worst-case handling
   388	    (_handle_worst) still fit (ILC-I7); otherwise the round handles what it has, oldest first, the first message always
   389	    (to completion, ack included, as far as the per-request guard admits each call). With the AWS adapters' worst
   390	    cases that rule admits one receive per round, so the slot received from first is chosen at random each round
   391	    (iss.rng): a fixed or schedule-derived first slot could keep receiving from the same (possibly empty) queue,
   392	    while a random one reaches every slot with probability 1, with no remembered state. Residual: if an invocation
   393	    cannot fit one receive plus one message's complete handling, progress waits for faster dependencies (the stated
   394	    capacity limit, DESIGN.md)."""
   395	    n, d = 0, _deadline(iss)
   396	    start = d.clock()
   397	
   398	    def over():
   399	        return d.clock() - start >= share_s or d.available() < MIN_REQUEST_S
   400	    slots = list(iss.signers.items())
   401	    receive_worst = max((_queue_worst(s) for _, s in slots), default=0)
   402	    handle_worst = max((_handle_worst(iss, s) for _, s in slots), default=0)
   403	    for _ in range(max_batches):
   404	        received = []
   405	        first = iss.rng.randrange(len(slots)) if slots else 0       # see the docstring: no parity, no state
   406	        for k_slot, (slot, signer) in enumerate(slots[first:] + slots[:first]):
   407	            i = (first + k_slot) % len(slots)
   408	            if k_slot and d.available() < receive_worst + handle_worst:
   409	                break                              # ILC-I7: keep room for one message's COMPLETE handling
   410	            try:
   411	                batch = signer.receive(10)
   412	            except OutOfBudget as e:
   413	                iss.note("drain: no time for the next receive:", slot, e)
   414	                break
   415	            received += [(age, i, j, slot, signer, handle, body) for j, (handle, body, age) in enumerate(batch)]
